/-- The six-operations package of the sketch, with every one of its eight clauses.
Source: literature/blueprint/latest/blueprint/part-duality-trace-formula/sec-poincare-duality/
sec-perfect-complexes-on-the-point-and-two-exchange-formulas/sk-def-ops/sk-thm-sf-package/
_section.md and sk-thm-sf-package.proof.md, clauses (1)--(8) (blueprint: sk-thm-sf-package).

Proof, following the eight steps of the node.
1. The ambient operations and Lf^* -| Rf_* are those of det-def-sf-operations. The
coefficient sheaves are cartesian (sk-prop-sfb-cartesian-coefficients), so Lf^* is exact
and preserves D^+; fix-prop-adjunctions gives units, counits and the D^+ Hom bijection,
and sk-rem-sf-typing the constructible restrictions. The finite exceptional adjoint is
the transported f^x (def-weil-exceptional-inverse-image); sk-thm-existence builds the
admissible constructible right adjoint (Brown); thm-sf-ambient-adjoint-class and
sk-prop-sf-rf-shriek-preservation give its adjunction and preservation. The full-CD
remark gives the conditional ambient boundary; det-def-sf-operations and sk-lem-sf-mate
normalize units, counits and composition mates.
2. For a Cartesian square det-prop-sf-cbc gives the typing of Ex_!, with identity,
compactification independence and composition on etale-origin complexes;
fix-lem-exchanges gives naturality, identity, pasting and refinement coherence. Proper
and smooth Ex_* are sk-thm-properbasechange and sk-thm-smooth-base-change, in finite D^+
form thm-weil-pbc-bounded-below and sbc-thm-bounded-below-derived-smooth-base-change,
transported by sk-prop-sf-comparison; the condensed forms are
sk-thm-sfb-proper-base-change and sk-thm-sbc-coefficients, with reduction mod pi_E,
integral models and finite descent through sk-prop-scalar-six; sk-prop-sf-comp-coherence
and sk-thm-sf-comp-composition transport the comparisons and the composition law.
3. det-thm-sf-pf-finite, sk-thm-sf-pf-proetale, sk-thm-sf-pf-adic, sk-thm-sf-pf-field and
det-prop-sf-pf-reduction make PF an isomorphism at every admissible coefficient;
sk-prop-sf-pf-coherence gives naturality, base-change compatibility and associativity.
4. Nagata compactification and its comparison category give compactifications;
sk-prop-sf-comp-coherence, sk-thm-sf-comp-composition and sk-prop-sf-comp-proper give
independence, R(gf)_! = Rg_! Rf_! and Rf_! = Rf_* for proper f.
5. sk-thm-smooth-purity gives the orientation isomorphism at finite coefficients;
sk-prop-cohsm its tensor form and base-change mate; sk-thm-purity-transport the
O_E, E and Qbar stages; sk-lem-sf-mate composition compatibility; the smooth step of
sk-thm-sf-kunneth-verdier identifies alpha with the pullback--tensor isomorphism.
6. det-prop-sf-biduality-general gives the anti-equivalence and biduality. For M in
Dctf, sk-thm-sf-tensor-hom, inverse PF and the two adjunctions identify
Hom(T, D_Y Rf_! M) with Hom(T, Rf_* D_X M); Yoneda gives epsilon
(sk-thm-sf-verdier-exchange). For X -> Y -> Z the two tensor--Hom chains are pasted by
the PF pentagon and base-change coherence (sk-prop-sf-pf-coherence), sk-lem-sf-mate and
fix-prop-coherence. sk-thm-sf-dual-perfect, sk-thm-sf-global-duality and
sk-thm-sf-identification, with sk-prop-sf-dualizable-biduality and
sk-lem-sf-twist-interchange, give theta_K, global duality and the Poincare pairing.
7. sk-thm-sf-kunneth-relative assembles composition, inverse projections and inverse
Ex_!, with sk-prop-sf-kunneth-ordinary; steps 2--4 and sk-prop-sf-pf-coherence give
symmetry, triple products, base change, projection and closed supports; the domains
are those of det-rem-sf-matrix.
8. sk-thm-sf-ctf-stability gives closure, sk-lem-sf-flat-model flat models;
det-thm-sf-direct-image-tor-amplitude gives [a,b+2d], sk-cor-sf-direct-image-ctf
constructibility, det-thm-sf-hom-ctf the Hom intervals, det-prop-sf-finiteness through
sk-prop-sf-comparison and sk-prop-sf-rf-shriek-preservation finiteness; the Rf^! shifts
[a,b+2d+1] and [a-2D,b+2dim Y+1] are clause (2) of thm-sf-preservation-class;
thm-sf-ctf-stability and det-rem-sf-matrix assemble the intervals. -/
theorem sixOperationsPackage (ell : ℕ) [Fact ell.Prime] (k : Type u) [Field k]
    (hk : Finite k ∨ IsAlgClosed k) [Fact (ringChar k ≠ ell)] :
    SixOperationsPackage ell k hk := by
  sorry

